; ============================================================
; TITLE:    Twinkle Twinkle Little Star
; CATEGORY: Music & Sound
; LEVEL:    Beginner
; TAGS:     song, data list, stars, property list
; SUMMARY:  Plays Twinkle Twinkle Little Star from a list of notes and draws a star in the night sky for every note, higher notes higher up.
; ============================================================
;
; WHAT IT DOES
;   The tune is stored as data: a list of little lists, each holding a
;   note name and how many beats it lasts. As each note plays, a star
;   appears in the sky. High notes make stars near the top, low notes
;   near the bottom, so the sky ends up drawing the shape of the tune.
;
; HOW TO USE
;   Press Run with the sound on. Change "make "beat 280" to change the
;   speed of the song.
;
; CONCEPTS YOU WILL LEARN
;   * storing a song as a list of [note beats] pairs
;   * FIRST and LAST take the parts out of each pair
;   * a property list turns note names into frequencies
;   * using a number (the pitch) to decide where to draw
;
; THINGS TO TRY
;   * The second half of the song is missing: "up above the world so
;     high". Add it: [g 1] [g 1] [f 1] [f 1] [e 1] [e 1] [d 2], twice.
;   * The same tune is the ABC song. Sing along!
;   * Make long notes draw bigger stars.
; ============================================================

pprop "pitch "c 262  pprop "pitch "d 294  pprop "pitch "e 330
pprop "pitch "f 349  pprop "pitch "g 392  pprop "pitch "a 440

; Twinkle twinkle little star, how I wonder what you are.
make "song [[c 1] [c 1] [g 1] [g 1] [a 1] [a 1] [g 2]
            [f 1] [f 1] [e 1] [e 1] [d 1] [d 1] [c 2]]

make "beat 280

; A five-pointed star of any size, filled with yellow.
to star :size
  filled 6 [repeat 5 [fd :size rt 144]]
end

; The height of a star depends on the pitch: 262 (low C) lands near
; the bottom of the sky and 440 (A) near the top.
to note.height :freq
  output (:freq - 262) * 2 - 120
end

to twinkle
  localmake "x -330
  foreach :song [
    localmake "freq gprop "pitch first ?
    penup setxy :x note.height :freq
    setheading 0 lt 18 pendown
    star 14 * last ?
    sound (list :freq :beat * last ?)
    make "x :x + 50
  ]
end

; A dark blue sky and a white moon to start with.
clearscreen
hideturtle
setbackground [10 15 50]
penup setxy 270 200 setheading 0 pendown
filled 7 [repeat 36 [fd 6 rt 10]]   ; a 36-sided circle
twinkle
